# Example identity terms for the release privacy gate.
#
# Copy this to .anon-identities (which is gitignored and never committed)
# and fill it in with YOUR real identity:
#
#     cp .anon-identities.example .anon-identities
#
# One regex per line. Comments start with '#'. The gate fails closed: with no
# terms file it refuses to pass, because "no terms" cannot prove anything is
# clean. A malformed regex also blocks the release rather than silently
# matching nothing.
#
# What to include, anything that could link a public artefact back to you:
#   * your real name and spelling variants
#   * your real email address and its domain
#   * your other/personal account handles on any platform
#   * local filesystem paths that contain your OS username
#   * names of private or personal projects
#   * any working notes or handoff documents that should not be public

# --- examples (replace or delete) ---
#\bYourRealName\b
#\bAnotherSurname\b
# you@yourdomain\.com
#\byourdomain\.com
# your-personal-handle
# /home/yourusername
# /Users/yourusername
# your-private-project
